meta {
  name: Update Bug Report (Empty Body)
  type: http
  seq: 5
}

patch {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/platform/bug-reports/{{bugReportId}}
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{platformAccessToken}}
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {}
}

tests {
  test("returns 400 Bad Request", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(400);
  });
}

docs {
  # PATCH /platform/bug-reports/:id — the empty-body guard

  A PATCH carrying neither `status` nor `internalNotes` is rejected rather than
  answered with the unchanged record. Silently succeeding would turn a client
  bug — a form that forgot to send its field — into a save button that appears
  to work and changes nothing.

  Enforced by a `.refine()` on the zod schema, so it is a `400` with a form-level
  error rather than a field-level one:

  ```json
  {
    "message": "Validation failed",
    "errors": {
      "formErrors": ["Provide a status or internal notes to update."],
      "fieldErrors": {}
    }
  }
  ```

  Note the asymmetry with `internalNotes: ""`, which is **valid** and clears the
  note. Omitting a field and sending it empty are deliberately different.
}
